 "reasoning": "CVE-2026-74666 is a published Linux-CNA kernel UAF/NULL-deref race in AF_PACKET ring reconfiguration versus pressure clearing; GHSA is not withdrawn, so this is a real vulnerability. The defective sink is the poll/recvmsg pressure-clearing path that trusts po->prot_hook.func to decide whether to walk tpacket ring storage, while packet_set_ring publishes that hook after releasing the lock that covers the ring swap. git log/parent-tree comparison shows that hook-after-unlock already existed at 9954729, but the pressure-clearing syscall path that creates this race was first written in 2ccdbaa6d55b (single-parent, non-squash, 2015 Willem de Bruijn). That commit is the kernel Fixes: target and the CVE git-range start, first appears in v4.2-rc1, and is absent from v4.1. Subsequent helper extraction and PACKET_SOCK_PRESSURE conversion are refactors, not first-writes. The direct fix is mainline 1a35da3, which closes the same mechanism by moving the hook assignment under the queue lock and locking recvmsg pressure clear; it lands in v7.2 and not v7.1, matching CVE fixed versions. AI is judged only from the BIC commit object: no AI/bot trailers or identities, so the verdict is NOT_AI. AI assistance on the 2026 fix is irrelevant to BIC authorship.",
