 "bug_semantics": "Authenticated SSE and stateful Streamable HTTP servers treated the client-supplied session key as the only authorization for attaching a request to an existing session. SseServerTransport.handle_post_message resolved request.query_params['session_id'] to a writer in _read_stream_writers and forwarded JSON-RPC without comparing scope['user'] to the creator. StreamableHTTPSessionManager._handle_stateful_request did the same with the Mcp-Session-Id header against _server_instances. A second bearer-authenticated principal who obtained the UUID could inject messages; SSE delivered results to the original event stream, while Streamable HTTP returned them to the injector. The 1.27.2 fix stores AuthorizationContext (OAuth client_id plus token iss/sub when present) at session creation and answers a mismatched principal with the same 404 as an unknown session.",
