 "bug_semantics": "openssl_encrypt/modules/json_validator.py optionally imports jsonschema and sets JSONSCHEMA_AVAILABLE=False on ImportError. SecureJSONValidator.validate_against_schema() then prints a warning and returns without raising, so schema validation is recorded as success. Callers such as secure_metadata_loads() -> validate_metadata() and the MED-8 wiring in crypt_utils.parse_metadata / crypt_core decryption accept attacker-controlled metadata, templates, or keystore JSON without schema checks. At introduction jsonschema was not declared in requirements.txt/pyproject.toml, so a missing or removed jsonschema package was a realistic environment. The same first-write also skip-returns from validate_metadata() on an unknown format_version even when jsonschema is present. Vendor GHSA-425g and CVE-2026-74875 map the patched boundary to 1.4.0, which fail-closes only the missing-jsonschema path.",
