13-20260926/execution/evidence/omni-secret-resource.stdout", "sha256": "8a2eb7128e9f55b21e5167456ac35987a31e43fe4f7dd148ccd82698487d39d1"}, {"path": "/home/hanqing/agents/ai-slop/research/r14-closeout-20260915/r1-vulnerability13-20260926/execution/evidence/omni-resource-callers.stdout", "sha256": "77ed395ec678920306f2b540b42f6f0a561823327cfaa3667cb391cf2797f46a"}, {"path": "/home/hanqing/agents/ai-slop/research/r14-closeout-20260915/r1-core-chain10-20260925-a2/execution/evidence/omni-shared-repair-diff.stdout", "sha256": "a7a2c46779d29da3b7948a27b4a3249661b8ff9c19c13f74eceea5a250f73c85"}, {"path": "/home/hanqing/agents/ai-slop/research/r14-closeout-20260915/r1-core-chain10-20260925-a2/execution/evidence/omni-signature-dependency.raw", "sha256": "1f9198cb7b5f8f72206daa28056692591a6634edfcc6818606b98ff53c878abf"}, {"path": "/home/hanqing/agents/ai-slop/research/r14-closeout-20260915/r1-public-followup13-20260924/execution/evidence/omni-information.raw.json", "sha256": "f80e41c6530b8a327a4fd2ea603ea2bc102e0a11719c89321c892cc84505ef3f"}, {"path": "/home/hanqing/agents/ai-slop/research/r14-closeout-20260915/r1-vulnerability13-20260926/execution/evidence/omni-runtime-response.stdout", "sha256": "91bffcfa33f0f0e8f28b24b1c7aeff7e24eae3e0d6610e833110d10625aeb71c"}, {"path": "/home/hanqing/agents/ai-slop/research/r14-closeout-20260915/r1-vulnerability13-20260926/execution/evidence/omni-runtime-validated-state.stdout", "sha256": "f76e6acc9f173185a78b64c4b1caa4dcc83982a26b0cc997d5db50b561cb3709"}, {"path": "/home/hanqing/agents/ai-slop/research/r14-closeout-20260915/r1-evidence-frontier10-20260925-a3/execution/evidence/omni-parent-state-access.stdout", "sha256": "6545b7b33c93dc5ff4991170952044706fe619726a6a23eeffb87ccedfe81b43"}], "input_completeness": {"missing_report_hold": false, "missing_reports": [], "note": "Both exact frozen reports are present and substantive. Legacy frozen-gate shape diagnostics are retained separately; presence is not a claim of clean strict-schema quality or research acceptance.", "reports_present": 2, "required_lanes": ["primary", "blind-r14"], "unfinished_reports": []}, "next_question": "The import positively contains the masking concern. It does not identify its original logical member or establish that this is the introduction of every signature-related information disclosure. Public deposit identity and advisory-mechanism allocation are separate questions. The saved file declares Sidero Labs copyright, and carrier metadata names human contributors. Neither assigns the original logical masking/authentication member or establishes marker coverage there. No positive AI attribution is established and no universal unaided-coding attestation is required. Which operation, protected field and unauthorized recipient does GHSA-77r9-w39m-9xh5 actually describe? The published description supplies none, the logging path acts on submitted data, and the inspected protected Get/List path enforces authorization before returning it. A vendor-bound disclosure trace or an already-published primary observation is the missing fact.", "resolutions": {"advisory": "Preserve the active keyed advisory and consulted aliases; a withdrawn duplicate does not reject a live keyed case.", "ai": "The saved file declares Sidero Labs copyright, and carrier metadata names human contributors. Neither assigns the original logical masking/authentication member or establishes marker coverage there. No positive AI attribution is established and no universal unaided-coding attestation is required.", "bic": "The import positively contains the masking concern. It does not identify its original logical member or establish that this is the introduction of every signature-related information disclosure. Public deposit identity and advisory-mechanism allocation are separate questions.", "fix": "5beb24f7d04e2e2469f796a2f32cf3a56b087528 flips sensitivity decode failures to mask, adds nil guards and moves recovery, and installs a required-signature callback with go-api-signature v0.3.8. Dependency 68478e2f57a3bca4345c6e189c0a4216dfb9b1ed converts required-but-missing signatures to invalid-signature errors. A subsequent internal-actor exception preserves the intentional local service. These component repairs can be explained independently; the sparse GHSA-77r9-w39m-9xh5 does not identify which data/recipient/operation its confidentiality claim concerns, so advisory-specific complete repair remains unknown.", "input_quality": "Both exact frozen lane inputs reviewed. Retain their observations as hypotheses; older missing schema fields and unsupported carrier-to-member/identity inferences do not become a new independent audit. Current source evidence and scoped conclusions above resolve the behavioral claims; original protocol gaps remain explicit.", "mechanism": "Logging: InterceptBodyToTags -> NewRewriter clones Create/Update requests -> isSensitiveSpec/isSensitiveResource decodes resource metadata -> failure returns false -> NewHook retains unmasked request -> grpc.request.content tag -> logging pipeline, with a 1024-byte body cap. This operates on the submitted request, not a database read. Signature: AuthConfig constructs a message without required-check options -> Signature gets ErrNotFound and continues without installing identity/role -> downstream auth.Check rejects operations requiring a role or signature. The missing early gate alone therefore does not prove arbitrary protected reads. The actual Get response path is ResourceServer.Get -> Runtime.Get -> cachedState.Get -> validated.State.Get -> authorizationValidationOptions/checkForRole -> filterAccess/auth.CheckGRPC. Validated.Get may load a resource internally before validation, but returns no resource to the caller if validation fails; Runtime.Get and ResourceServer.Get return the error before MarshalJSON. List validates before listing. For auth-enabled protected kinds, missing role/signature is rejected. Intentional auth-disabled and internal-actor paths are not evidence of unauthorized disclosure. Source-supported request-secret retention in logs when classification fails and the retained serialized prefix contains the secret. Correctly decoded ConfigPatch explicitly declares meta.Sensitive and is masked, contradicting the broad claim that all normal sensitive resources leak. An unauthorized remote recipient of existing stored secrets is not established by these two mechanisms alone.", "residual": "The import positively contains the masking concern. It does not identify its original logical member or establish that this is the introduction of every signature-related information disclosure. Public deposit identity and advisory-mechanism allocation are separate questions. The saved file declares Sidero Labs copyright, and carrier metadata names human contributors. Neither assigns the original logical masking/authentication member or establishes marker coverage there. No positive AI attribution is established and no universal unaided-coding attestation is required. Which operation, protected field and unauthorized recipient does GHSA-77r9-w39m-9xh5 actually describe? The published description supplies none, the logging path acts on submitted data, and the inspected protected Get/List path enforces authorization before returning it. A vendor-bound disclosure trace or an already-published primary observation is the missing fact.", "versions": "v1.0.2 and v1.1.5 contain corrected resource.go/auth_config blob identities and source grep confirms fail-closed masking. Prior branch carriers 1fd954af/1396083f remain distinguished from direct 5beb24f7. Shipping these parts does not settle which minimum subset addresses this advisory."}, "reviewed_dimensions": ["advisory", "mechanism", "bic", "ai", "fix", "versions", "residual"], "sha256": {"accepted": "646a21409d355d6850dbe984d8ec85dc4cbb9b67f7fee130b65ee7832e6b4dd0", "blind-r14": "56c8499fee19ea00b7a14f116bbdce471d88b79081bbb4ff8a37cc8606a5444f", "primary": "2213f79889489c95c1ce3d458c09daf91a4759d02eb48632c7128596294508db"}, "status": "BLOCKED", "verdict": "EVIDENCE_GAP"}}

