 "bug_semantics": "When generating models from XML Schema, _XMLSchemaConverter walks xs:include, xs:import, xs:redefine, and (later) xs:override children and treats attacker-controlled schemaLocation as a filesystem path. It computes location = (source_dir / schema_location).resolve(), which collapses ../ and accepts absolute paths, then reads the target with location.read_text() (later _read_xml_text -> path.read_bytes()) after only an is_file() check. Included type names, restrictions, and enumerations are folded into generated Python. There is no is_relative_to(self.base_path) gate and no allow_remote_refs control on this path, so --no-allow-remote-refs does not mitigate it. The same unbounded read was later duplicated in _detect_effective_xmlschema_version. CPython ElementTree does not fetch external entities, so this is path traversal / local file read (CWE-22/CWE-200), not XXE.",
