 "bug_semantics": "SctpMessageCompletionHandler reassembles incomplete SCTP DATA chunks per streamIdentifier. For every non-complete fragment it stored fragments.put(streamIdentifier, Unpooled.wrappedBuffer(previousAccumulator, newSlice)), creating a new CompositeByteBuf whose first component is the previous composite. After N fragments the readableBytes()/getBytes() path recurses N levels, and each layer retains component arrays. There was no cap on fragment count N, total buffered bytes, or distinct streamIdentifiers (each map entry is an independent nested chain). A remote peer that never sets the complete flag can force unbounded nested composites from 1-byte chunks, exhausting memory/stack (CWE-770 DoS). The 2026 fix stores a flat List<ByteBuf> per stream, enforces maxIncompleteSctpMessages and maxFragments (default 128), and builds one CompositeByteBuf only when the message completes.",
