 "bug_semantics": "An attacker uploads a file whose filename extension passes fileUpload.fileExtensions (default excludes HTML; e.g. evil.txt) while sending Content-Type text/html (REST header or JSON _ContentType). FilesRouter validates the extension independently of MIME and forwards the user Content-Type into FilesController.createFile. Before the fix, createFile only derived MIME from the filename when contentType was missing; if both extension and Content-Type were present, the user MIME was stored. Adapters that persist and serve that header (S3, GCS) then deliver the body as text/html, enabling stored XSS / content-type confusion (CWE-436). Parse Server's own GET path and GridFS derive Content-Type from the filename at serve time, so the default adapter is not a sink.",
