 "bug_semantics": "Apache ActiveMQ Classic authorization is supposed to require the destination admin ACL to create or delete queues/topics. A client destroyDestination() sends OpenWire DestinationInfo REMOVE, which the broker dispatches to AuthorizationBroker.removeDestinationInfo (and removeDestination). After AMQ-3851 those methods shared checkDestinationAdmin, which returned true whenever the destination already existed and therefore never consulted admin ACLs on the only case that matters for deletion. Any authenticated connection could delete existing destinations it was not permitted to administer (DoS/availability). The 2026 fix keeps the add short-circuit (skip admin if dest exists) and inverts it for remove (skip admin only if dest does not exist; require admin if it does).",
