 "bug_semantics": "In the rtl2832_sdr V4L2 SDR driver, vb2 delivers capture buffers to rtl2832_sdr_buf_queue() (list_add_tail onto dev->queued_bufs) before it calls rtl2832_sdr_start_streaming(). That start callback can fail on missing USB device (-ENODEV), interrupted v4l2_lock (-ERESTARTSYS), or any of six setup steps (subdev s_power/tuner, tuner frequency, ADC, stream-buffer alloc, URB alloc, URB submit). Those paths returned the error without vb2_buffer_done() on the already-owned queued buffers, so vb2_start_streaming() hits WARN_ON(owned_by_drv_count), the buffers leak, and later URB completion or buf_queue list_add_tail can operate on freed vb2 objects (local ioctl UAF). The original function also fell through a shared err label on success, so cleanup could not be added there without an explicit success return.",
