 "bug_semantics": "MessagePack typeless deserialization (ext type 100) lets the payload name a .NET type. TypelessFormatter resolves that name and, starting in 2019, calls MessagePackSerializerOptions.ThrowIfDeserializingTypeIsDisallowed before constructing a formatter. The default implementation compared only the outer type.FullName to a small DisallowedTypes set (and any user override of the virtual method likewise saw only the wrapper). An attacker who can submit typeless data can therefore send a blocked gadget as T[] or List<T> (or another constructed generic): the wrapper name is not on the list, the check returns, and the formatter pipeline still instantiates formatters for the inner blocked type. That is CWE-470/CWE-502 weakening of the advertised type-restriction hook, not a new gadget by itself. The 2026 fix keeps the leaf check in ThrowIfDeserializingTypeIsDisallowedCore and recursively walks array/pointer/byref element types and constructed generic arguments before formatter resolution.",
