 "bug_semantics": "Mercurius serves GraphQL over HTTP at /graphql. A CORS-simple request can include cookies without an OPTIONS preflight. In v16.3.0 the GET handler reads query/variables from the query string and executes GraphQL, so a cross-origin GET /graphql?query=... with credentials can run authenticated queries (and any query with side effects). The GHSA/CVE text and PoC instead describe Fastify mis-parsing application/x-www-form-urlencoded, multipart/form-data, or text/plain as application/json on POST. Mercurius 16 depends on Fastify 5, whose default JSON parser matches only application/json (plus parameters); urlencoded/multipart yield 415 and text/plain is a string, so that POST PoC does not execute GraphQL on the v16 stack. Mercurius itself only extra-parses application/graphql. The vendor fix is Apollo-style CSRF prevention: require a non-simple Content-Type or a custom header so the browser must preflight. POST application/json already preflights; GET was the Mercurius-owned simple-request sink in the affected v16 range.",
