 "bug_semantics": "When FILE_UPLOAD_DIRECTORY_PERMISSIONS / FileSystemStorage.directory_permissions_mode is set, Django created intermediate directories by temporarily calling os.umask() in the current thread, then os.makedirs(), then restoring umask. FileBasedCache._createdir used the same process-wide umask(0o077) pattern to force 0o700. os.umask is process-global, so a concurrent thread handling another request can mkdir/open while the mask is wrong, producing files or directories with unintended permissions (CWE-362). Source is attacker-controlled concurrent requests that trigger storage saves or file-cache writes; sink is kernel file-creation permission bits. The 2026 fix stops mutating umask and applies the requested mode with os.chmod after os.mkdir.",
