 "bug_semantics": "devalue.parse JSON.parses a payload into a values array, then unflatten/hydrate walks it. Plain-object records are rebuilt with `for (const key in value) { object[key] = hydrate(value[key]); }` on a normal `{}`. A crafted key `__proto__` therefore hits Object.prototype.__proto__ and installs a new prototype, so later own properties (including getters such as magnitude in the GHSA Vector PoC) can be overwritten. Property values that are strings rather than numeric indices are passed to hydrate; because hydrate used `index in hydrated` / `values[index]` on an Array without requiring typeof index === 'number', strings such as `push` or `toString` resolve to Array.prototype methods and get assigned onto the revived object (GHSA PoC `[{ \"toString\":\"push\" }]`). Attacker-controlled serialized input is the source; polluted prototypes and hijacked methods on the parsed object are the sink (CWE-1321).",
