 "bug_semantics": "django.contrib.admin.utils.display_for_field() special-cased models.URLField by emitting format_html('<a href=\"{}\">{}</a>', value, value) using the raw stored field value as the href. Admin changelist cells and read-only change-form widgets call this helper, so a stored unsafe scheme (javascript:, data:, etc.) became a clickable link for staff. URLField form/admin validation already rejects those schemes, so the practical source is persistence that skips model validation (queryset writes, deserialization, bulk import). Clicking the link is XSS in the authenticated admin session (CWE-83). The 2026 fix runs URLValidator() first and falls back to plain text on ValidationError. This is a new display_for_field sink from the 5.2 #36032 feature, not leftover AdminURLFieldWidget XSS from CVE-2019-12308.",
