 "bug_semantics": "On the self-hosted Next.js Node server, WebSocket upgrade requests are handled by upgradeHandler in packages/next/src/server/lib/router-server.ts. resolveRoutes parses req.url (including HTTP absolute-form targets such as GET http://127.0.0.1:internal/secret HTTP/1.1) and returns parsedUrl.protocol whenever that URL has a scheme. Before the fix, the upgrade path proxied with proxyRequest/httpxy as soon as parsedUrl.protocol was set, without requiring that routing had finished an explicit external rewrite (finished) and without rejecting redirect statusCodes. That lets an untrusted client force the origin to open a WebSocket/HTTP proxy to an arbitrary internal or external host, including cloud metadata, which is CWE-918 SSRF. The ordinary HTTP request handler already gated proxying on finished && parsedUrl.protocol, so the same absolute-form request was not treated as a safe rewrite on that path. The May 2026 guard applies those same checks to upgrades: proxy only when finished && parsedUrl.protocol && !statusCode, otherwise end the socket. Configured ws/http external rewrites still work because they set finished without a redirect statusCode.",
