 "bug_semantics": "Fickling's MLAllowlist pass is supposed to flag pickle imports outside ML_ALLOWLIST, including standard-library modules that the UnsafeImports denylist never lists. AnalysisContext.shorten_code() is a formatter that also records each shortened snippet in a process-wide reported_shortened_code set. UnsafeImportsML walks every import and calls shorten_code() even when the import is not unsafe, so every import is marked reported. When MLAllowlist later walks the same nodes, already_reported is true and it continues without consulting ML_ALLOWLIST. check_safety() therefore returns LIKELY_SAFE for payloads such as from ast import parse. fickling.load() treats LIKELY_SAFE as permission to pickle.loads(), so the payload runs. UnsafeImportsML and MLAllowlist are each consistent in isolation; the defect is the shared mutable dedup set plus the allowlist iterating the same full import set the poisoner already marked.",
