 "bug_semantics": "When the Vitest UI/API (or Browser Mode) HTTP server is listening, RPC handlers can write a test file and execute it. writeFile was introduced as an unauthenticated WebSocket handler that called fs.writeFile; rerun already executed tests. Combined, any client that can talk to the API can overwrite a test and run arbitrary script (CWE-862). On Windows, GET /__vitest_attachment__?path=... additionally used Vite's isFileServingAllowed without cleanUrl, so \\\\?\\\\..\\\\ bypassed the FS allow-list and streamed files outside the project (CWE-22). The 4.1.0/3.2.5 mitigation does not remove those handlers; it defaults api.allowWrite and api.allowExec to false whenever api.host is a non-loopback bind, and switches several FS checks to isFileLoadingAllowed/slash.",
