 "bug_semantics": "withCredentials (BindingStep) binds credential plaintext into the Pipeline body environment. ConsoleLogFilter/MaskingOutputStream redacts those values on the build console stream, but Pipeline failures persist the Throwable on flow ErrorAction and print it with Functions.printThrowable, which does not pass through ConsoleLogFilter. A body that interpolates a bound secret into error()/Exception (or any nested/suppressed cause) therefore writes the secret to the build log and stores it unmasked on the run. Attackers with permission to read that log (Jenkins advisory CVSS PR:L) recover the credential. The 2025 fix installs a FailureHandler that, when the printed throwable matches the secret pattern, rethrows MaskedException copies whose messages have secrets replaced with asterisks, including cause and suppressed chains.",
