 "bug_semantics": "In publish mode the kernel mux serves several workspace directories as static HTTP routes behind model.CheckAuth only. CheckAuth treats a publish JWT RoleReader as authenticated, and the publish proxy injects that JWT for reader accounts or, when Publish.Auth.Enable is false, for the anonymous account. GET /templates/<file>.md therefore returns user-authored template Markdown to a reader, while POST /api/file/getFile {\"path\":\"data/templates/<file>.md\"} is refused by refuseToAccess for non-administrators. The same CheckAuth-only gap exposes /snippets/* (JS/CSS by name), whole /widgets/, /plugins/, and /emojis/ trees, and /export/* artifacts that lack the publish-path gate /assets/* already had. Confidentiality-only CWE-862: missing authorization on static routes relative to REST/publish-access policy.",
