 "bug_semantics": "univ.Real stores ASN.1 REAL as (mantissa, base, exponent). Real.__float__ computed float(mantissa * pow(base, exponent)) with exact big-integer exponentiation. prettyPrint, str, comparisons, arithmetic, and int() all funnel through float(self). A compact BER/CER/DER REAL (or Real((m, b, e)) constructed directly) can encode a huge exponent; pow() then tries to materialize an enormous integer and the process hangs (CWE-400). Decoding itself only builds the tuple; the DoS fires on conversion. The 2011 RealDecoder left binary REAL as pass; binary encoding/decoding landed later (ae6f36fe, 2011-03-15 parent of the inf wrap) and still produced unbounded exponents that the same __float__ consumed. Fix in 0.6.4: base-2 via math.ldexp, base-10 overflow-checked against sys.float_info.max_10_exp so out-of-range values raise OverflowError and prettyPrint stays '<overflow>' without huge intermediates.",
