 "bug_semantics": "When ospfd has 'debug ospf packet ... detail' enabled, LS Update processing dumps each LSA. For opaque types, ospf_dump.c calls ospf_opaque_lsa_dump(), which invokes show_opaque_info_detail(NULL, &lsa, NULL). That dispatcher looks up the opaque-type functab and calls show_opaque_info with vty==NULL. Extended Link/Prefix show callbacks in ospfd/ospf_ext.c (registered as ospf_ext_link_show_info / ospf_ext_pref_show_info) then execute vty_out(vty, ...) and check_tlv_size's vty_out without testing vty, dereferencing a NULL vty and crashing ospfd (DoS). TE/RI callbacks already honored the NULL-vty dump contract; the CVE names show_opaque_info_detail because it is the dispatch frame, but the dereference is in the EXT show path it calls. The NVD-linked 0042fbe rewrite of already-present functab NULL checks does not stop this crash.",
