 "bug_semantics": "Applications that install DelegatingDecompressorFrameListener decompress HTTP/2 DATA via an EmbeddedChannel. Http2Decompressor.decompress() (and historically onDataRead) does decompressor.writeInbound(data.retain()). Java evaluates data.retain() before writeInbound, bumping ByteBuf refCnt 1->2. EmbeddedChannel.writeInbound begins with ensureOpen(); if cleanup()/finish() already closed the channel (stream removal or END_STREAM with the decompressor property still attached), ClosedChannelException is thrown before the pipeline takes ownership, so the decoder finally-release never runs. The surrounding catch rethrows Http2Exception/streamError without data.release(), so the extra reference is never dropped. The frame reader then releases once (refCnt 2->1) and the typically direct buffer is leaked. Repeating DATA on a long-lived connection exhausts direct memory (CWE-400/401 DoS).",
