 "bug_semantics": "Scriban's recursive-descent expression parser treats nested parentheses as ScriptNestedExpression nodes. ParseParenthesis consumes '(' and immediately calls ExpectAndParseExpression, which re-enters ParseExpression; each nesting level consumes native stack. Through 6.5.8, ParserOptions.ExpressionDepthLimit is a nullable int defaulting to null, and EnterExpression only logs when that option is set, so the PoC template {{ ((((...1...)))) }} with thousands of parens reaches an uncatchable StackOverflowException and kills the host process (CWE-674 DoS). 6.6.0 turns on a default of 250 at EnterExpression (`ExpressionDepthLimit ?? 250`) so the existing depth counter fires without an explicit caller setting.",
