 "bug_semantics": "Nomad workload-identity ACL policies can be attached to a specific job. Claim resolution called StateStore.ACLPolicyByJob, which queried the acl_policy memdb table with index name \"job_prefix\" rather than the exact \"job\" index. go-memdb prefix scans return every policy whose (namespace, jobID) key starts with the requested pair, so a job whose ID is a prefix of another job's ID (example: policy bound to test-job is also applied to test-job-2). The extra policies are merged into the workload token, incorrectly assigning privileges and allowing policy shadowing. The 1.10.2 fix performs an exact-match Get on index \"job\".",
