 "bug_semantics": "selinux_sctp_bind_connect() is the SELinux implementation of security_sctp_bind_connect(). From its first write it copies sk->sk_socket into a struct socket * and passes that pointer into selinux_socket_bind() and selinux_socket_connect_helper(), which immediately load sock->sk and never otherwise need the socket object. SCTP Dynamic Address Reconfiguration (ASCONF ADD_IP/SET_PRIMARY) invokes the same hook from net/sctp/sm_make_chunk.c on asoc->ep->base.sk in the receive/softirq path. After userspace close(), sk->sk_socket can already be NULL while associations still process authenticated ASCONF chunks, so the SELinux hook NULL-dereferences sk_socket and oopses/panics the host. setsockopt bindx/connectx/set_primary and sendmsg-connect hold a file reference and are not the crashing path. The 2026 fix stops touching sk_socket by teaching the bind/connect helpers to take struct sock * directly.",
