 "bug_semantics": "Spring Security 7 maps HttpSecurity.securityMatcher(String...) (advisory wording: securityMatchers(String)) through a PathPatternRequestMatcher.Builder shared object. HttpSecurityConfiguration.createSharedObjects() always constructed a default PathPatternRequestMatcherBuilderFactoryBean with no basePath, so a published PathPatternRequestMatcher.Builder bean that prepends a servlet path (the Spring Boot spring.mvc.servlet.path pattern) was ignored. A chain configured as securityMatcher(\"/admin/**\") therefore matched /admin/** instead of /<servlet-path>/admin/**. Intended requests missed that filter chain, so authentication, authorization, and other security components were not applied (CWE-693). authorizeHttpRequests/requestMatchers(String) via AbstractRequestMatcherRegistry already used getIfUnique on the bean after aeb2dbc; the broken path is the securityMatcher(String...) shared-object lookup.",
