 "bug_semantics": "Kiota's C# generator copies attacker-controlled OpenAPI text (operation/schema/parameter description; later also externalDocs.description as DocumentationLabel and externalDocs.url as DocumentationLink) into generated single-line /// XML documentation comments. The C# writer prefixes each WriteLine with '/// ' but, until the 2026 fix, only XML-escaped the payload (CleanupXMLString) and never stripped line terminators. A newline in the OpenAPI field terminates the comment; the remainder is emitted at namespace/type scope and is compiled when a developer or CI builds the generated client. CleanupDescription (from 2022) stripped only [\\r\\n\\t] at some CodeDOM assignment sites, so Unicode NEL/LS/PS in descriptions still reached the sink, and ExternalDocs label/link never went through CleanupDescription at all. Practical preconditions are an untrusted or tampered OpenAPI description used as generation input.",
