 "bug_semantics": "picklescan is a pickle/PyTorch-model scanner whose security control is a module/name denylist. It disassembles pickle opcodes, collects GLOBAL/STACK_GLOBAL imports, and marks a global Dangerous only if the module is in the denylist and the name matches (\"*\" or an explicit set). timeit.timeit() is a stdlib helper that execs/evals the supplied statement (and can therefore import os and run os.system). Before 0.0.25 the denylist had no \"timeit\" entry, so a payload class whose __reduce__ returns (timeit.timeit, ('', 'import os; os.system(...)')) is classified Suspicious or not reported at all; issues_count and infected_files stay 0; the CLI summary shows a clean scan; pickle.load() then executes the statement. Source: incomplete _suspicious_globals/_unsafe_globals. Sink: _build_scan_result_from_raw_globals / original scan_pickle_bytes lookup that only increments issues for listed names. Attack path: attacker ships a malicious .pkl/.pt; victim trusts picklescan; victim deserializes.",
