 "bug_semantics": "Spring Security one-time-token login authenticates by calling OneTimeTokenService.consume(); a successful consume must be single-use. JdbcOneTimeTokenService.consume() issues an auto-commit SELECT (selectOneTimeToken) and, if a row exists, a separate auto-commit DELETE (deleteOneTimeToken) whose jdbcOperations.update rowcount is discarded; it then returns the already-loaded token unless isExpired(). Two concurrent /login/ott submissions with the same valid token can both pass the SELECT before either DELETE commits, both treat consume as success, and both establish sessions. InMemoryOneTimeTokenService is unaffected because ConcurrentHashMap.remove is atomic. Attack requires explicit oneTimeTokenLogin() plus an explicit JdbcOneTimeTokenService bean.",
