 "bug_semantics": "DotGit treats a Git reference name as a relative filesystem path under the repository's .git directory. SetRef writes the loose-ref file with d.fs.Create(r.Name().String()) (later fileName := r.Name().String() into setRef); Ref reads via readReferenceFile(\".\", name.String()); RemoveRef deletes via d.fs.Join(\".\", name.String()). Because the name is not required to stay under refs/ (or a one-level [A-Z_] pseudo-ref) and is not stripped of '.'/'..'/NTFS/HFS disguises, a name such as refs/heads/../../config or a mapped refs/remotes/origin/../../config resolves to .git/config. A malicious Git server can advertise such a name; clone/fetch refspec mapping can preserve the traversal. Only filesystem-backed storage/filesystem/dotgit is affected; storage/memory never turns names into paths. The 2026 patches add validReferenceName (IsSafe plus control-character and NTFS/HFS hardening) at those storage entry points and reject ErrReferenceNameEscape before any path join.",
