 "bug_semantics": "write_file and patch in hermes-agent refuse writes to sensitive system prefixes by calling _check_sensitive_path. That helper resolves the user path with os.path.realpath and then tests whether the resolved string starts with /etc/, /boot/, or /usr/lib/systemd/. On macOS /etc is a symlink to /private/etc, so a write to /etc/hosts (or a symlink whose realpath is under /private/etc) becomes /private/etc/hosts, which does not start with /etc/, and the checker returns None. The write then proceeds at OS permission level. Issue #8734 reproduced this through the API server: write_file('/etc/hosts') was not policy-blocked on Darwin while /boot/grub.cfg was. The same list also omitted /private/var (macOS /var symlink). This is CWE-59: the blocklist is applied to a fully resolved path without including the platform's resolved sensitive prefixes (and without also matching the unresolved path).",
