 "bug_semantics": "The backend Table widget partial emits the unsanitized GET parameter search into an HTML raw-text <script type=\"text/template\"> block as value=\"<?= get('search') ?>\". Attribute quotes are not a parser boundary there, so a crafted query containing a literal </script> (including mixed-case or whitespace variants) terminates the template early and injects markup/script into an authenticated backend page. get() is not HTTP-method-restricted, and the template is rendered even when searching is disabled, so any Table/DataTable page is a sink (in core, Editor Settings gated by backend.manage_editor). The 1.2.14 fix HTML-encodes the value with e() so the terminator cannot appear as raw text.",
