  "bug_semantics": "In @langchain/langgraph-checkpoint-redis, RedisSaver.list() and ShallowRedisSaver.list() build a RediSearch query by concatenating filter clauses. String filters were interpolated as (@${key}:{${value}}) with no escaping of RediSearch syntax. An attacker who can supply list()/getStateHistory() filter values (typical of user-facing history APIs) can inject | (OR) and braces, e.g. source=\"x}) | (@thread_id:{*\", producing (@thread_id:{victim}) (@source:{x}) | (@thread_id:{*}). RediSearch AND-binds tighter than OR, so the second clause matches every thread and returns other tenants' checkpoint documents from ft.search on the checkpoints index. The 1.0.2 patch escapes filter keys and values via escapeRediSearchTagValue before interpolation.",
