er. Original primary and blind-r14 hypotheses, including the superseded choice, are pinned in the case report and history.", "fix": "Current resolution: fix_sha=d257e5f36cfa9328600c8bde6f0de09a6ad9b6f4; direct_fix_sha=d257e5f36cfa9328600c8bde6f0de09a6ad9b6f4; atomic_repair_sha=None; AI_ROOT_CAUSE: PR #1099 explicitly names the model and describes the embedded PTY feature. Its first member f6664ea28525a0ba491b9355b4be6be3b5b549fe introduces the backend and routes; subsequent listed members change terminal presentation. The causal source is the original member, not the later Hermes Agent cherry-pick identity. With password/passkey auth disabled, remote callers reach PTY creation/input through normal routes. d257e5f36cfa9328600c8bde6f0de09a6ad9b6f4 applies the local-origin gate to all five terminal operations in 0.51.788. The declaration concerns this submitted feature and supports AI-assisted origin despite the member having a named human author and no trailer. Original primary and blind-r14 hypotheses, including the superseded choice, are pinned in the case report and history.", "versions": "Current resolution: Cherry-pick carrier 60a4cb05 is an ancestor of v0.50.237^{commit}=72b4ff66f0038413972477953b3eeae0b458410f (batch PR #1243 lists #1099 embedded terminal) and of v0.51.787. | 60a4cb05 is not an ancestor of v0.50.236. First affected tagged release is v0.50.237; CVE CNA range '0 < 0.51.788' overstates versions before the terminal feature existed. | d257e5f36cfa9328600c8bde6f0de09a6ad9b6f4 is not an ancestor of v0.51.787^{commit}=ef02ffec6d956a7d13a9cbe55bb2a663b8962495. | It is an ancestor of annotated tag v0.51.788^{commit}=df20e3f7d8133af8ca70537536244d37379c876f (release notes: 'embedded-terminal access hardening (#5268)'). First tags containing the gate: v0.51.788 and later. Original primary and blind-r14 hypotheses, including the superseded choice, are pinned in the case report and history.", "residual": "Current resolution: No decisive factual dependency ad