 "bug_semantics": "CVE-2024-58135/GHSA-3r5v-gmfp-3mh9 is CWE-338 in Mojolicious, not hashcat. From 7.28, `mojo generate app` writes a default HMAC session secret using Perl's non-crypto rand() mixed with PID and steady_time (later factored into Mojo::Util::generate_secret(), which still fell back to sha1_sum($$ . steady_time() . rand) without CryptX). That value is stored in the generated app config and used to HMAC-sign session cookies, so the keyspace is brute-forceable and sessions can be forged. hashcat/hashcat only appears because CPANSec tagged PR #4090 as an exploit: it adds hash-mode 16501 ('Perl Mojolicious session cookie (HMAC-SHA256, >= v9.19)') to recover those secrets. That is attack tooling against Mojolicious cookies, not a hashcat vulnerability.",
