 "bug_semantics": "NRF's unauthenticated OAuth2 token endpoint POST /oauth2/token parses application/x-www-form-urlencoded bodies by reflecting over models.NrfAccessTokenAccessTokenReq (historically models.AccessTokenReq). String and NF-type fields are SetString(); every other matched yaml-tag field is json.Unmarshal'd into a models.PlmnId and assigned with reflect.Value.Set. When the real field type is a slice ([]PlmnId, []Snssai, []PlmnIdNid, []string) or a different pointer (*PlmnIdNid), Go panics with 'reflect.Set: value of type *models.PlmnId is not assignable to type ...'. Gin recovery converts the panic to HTTP 500 without killing the process, so a remote client can repeatedly trigger expensive stack-trace panics on the token-issuance path. This is parser type-confusion (CWE-843) plus missing input-type validation (CWE-20), not an auth bypass.",
