 "bug_semantics": "uutils rm implements --preserve-root (default) by testing whether the command-line path string looks like '/'. From first implementation that was filename != \"/\", later rewritten as path.has_root() && path.parent().is_none() in handle_dir. A symlink such as /tmp/rootlink -> / has a parent component, so is_root is false; rm -rf --preserve-root /tmp/rootlink/ (or an equivalent path that is a directory after following the link) therefore recursively removes through the link into the real root tree. GNU rm instead caches /'s device/inode and compares directories it enters. The 2026 fix adds is_root_path() that still accepts a literal '/', but also canonicalizes so a symlink (or nested symlink) to / is treated as root and rejected when preserve_root and recursive are set.",
