 "bug_semantics": "mruby's compiler scope_new zero-initializes codegen_scope (nregs=0), then sets the stack pointer and nlocals to the local-variable count plus self without assigning nregs. nregs is only raised later if push() runs nregs_update (if sp > nregs). scope_finish copies the possibly-zero nregs into the irep (uint16_t). A nested class/module body executed via OP_EXEC does stack_extend(irep->nregs) then stack_clear(regs+1, irep->nregs-1). When nregs is 0, the uint16_t subtraction wraps to 65535, so stack_clear writes past the 128-slot (1024-byte) VM stack allocated by stack_init, which is the ASan heap-buffer-overflow in #6509.",
