 "bug_semantics": "On Unix recursive copy (-R/-r/-a) without --copy-contents, uu_cp treats character and block device nodes as stream sources. is_stream(metadata) is true for fifo||char||block. copy_helper recreates sockets and FIFOs in that mode but, before the fix, had no mknod path for devices, so copy_on_write called copy_stream: open the device, splice/read its bytes, and write them into a newly created regular file. That destroys device identity (a copied /dev/null is an empty regular file; major/minor are lost) and can hang or fill the disk when the source is an unbounded node such as /dev/zero. GNU cp instead mknods the destination unless --copy-contents is set. Non-recursive cp of a device as a file remains intended GNU behavior.",
