 blind-r14 hypotheses, including the superseded choice, are pinned in the case report and history.", "ai": "Current resolution: AI_CODE_FLAWED under the frozen contract: the earliest observed human command-construction boundary is 33ebe7acec14b25c5f84f35a664803fcab2f7781. The later GPT 5.6-authored 701ce32fe5ba8cb622c0e0342a376a6beb47d738 adds default-deny option checks but lists only --upload-pack for ls-remote; its equivalent --exec spelling remains accepted. Caller-controlled options can therefore still select an external program unless the wrapper rejects that spelling. This is an incomplete AI-assisted guard, not the first creation of the command builder. 1b0d2d9b91575f7db44ef4ff58ac37fc9335e5f6 adds --exec to that denylist in 3.1.59. The explicit allow_unsafe_options opt-in remains an intentional capability. Restoring the original human boundary separates origin from the admitted later flawed contribution; no later contract migration applies. Original primary and blind-r14 hypotheses, including the superseded choice, are pinned in the case report and history.", "fix": "Current resolution: fix_sha=1b0d2d9b91575f7db44ef4ff58ac37fc9335e5f6; direct_fix_sha=1b0d2d9b91575f7db44ef4ff58ac37fc9335e5f6; atomic_repair_sha=None; AI_CODE_FLAWED under the frozen contract: the earliest observed human command-construction boundary is 33ebe7acec14b25c5f84f35a664803fcab2f7781. The later GPT 5.6-authored 701ce32fe5ba8cb622c0e0342a376a6beb47d738 adds default-deny option checks but lists only --upload-pack for ls-remote; its equivalent --exec spelling remains accepted. Caller-controlled options can therefore still select an external program unless the wrapper rejects that spelling. This is an incomplete AI-assisted guard, not the first creation of the command builder. 1b0d2d9b91575f7db44ef4ff58ac37fc9335e5f6 adds --exec to that denylist in 3.1.59. The explicit allow_unsafe_options opt-in remains an intentional capability. Restoring the original human boundary separates origin from the admitted later flawed contribution; no later contract migration applies. Original primary and blind-r14 hypotheses, including the superseded choice, are pinned in the case report and history.", "versions": "Current resolution: Vendor range is GitPython pip <= 3.1.50 (no lower bound), matching an original-from-inception defect. | git merge-base --is-ancestor 33ebe7acec14b25c5f84f35a664803fcab2f7781 3.1.50 succeeds. Tag 3.1.50^{commit}=5a294a6fc7ed5dc0946d4b576257bf926178f269 still has the unguarded archive/iter_commits/blame/ls_remote paths and check_unsafe_options only on clone/fetch/pull/push. | BIC is also contained in the earliest tag 0.1.4 (924da9604d6474fd1be99dffdcc539eaaaa31626). | Vendor first_patched_version=3.1.51. Tag 3.1.51^{commit}=7b0764d309334b0f27f503d7fa1a395cbd165de0 ('bump to v3.1.51'). | git merge-base --is-ancestor 701ce32fe5ba8cb622c0e0342a376a6beb47d738 3.1.51 succeeds; git merge-base --is-ancestor 701ce32fe5ba8cb622c0e0342a376a6beb47d738 3.1.50 fails. | git tag --contains 701ce32 starts at 3.1.51. Merge af027be78693962c233cc989915f40e9b135f3a5 (PR #2163) is also an ancestor of 3.1.51. Release notes for 3.1.51 list 'guard unsafe git command options' (#2163). Original primary and blind-r14 hypotheses, including the superseded choice, are pinned in the case report and history.", "residual": "Current resolution: git ls-remote --exec stayed exploitable in 3.1.51-3.1.58 after the advertised 3.1.51 guard; closed by 1b0d2d9b in 3.1.59 Original primary and blind-r14 hypotheses, including the superseded choice, are pinned in the case report and history.", "input_quality": "Both original lane bytes and hashes are unchanged. Legacy shape or inference defects do not become new independent reports. The current proposal and primary observations resolve the affected fields; unresolved content remains BLOCKED."}, "reviewed_dimensions": ["advisory", "mechanism", "bic", "ai", "fix", "versions", "residual"], "sha256": {"accepted": "c629937ec576ec1cb62c65ff4