 "bug_semantics": "On CUSTOM_ROLES-licensed instances, DELETE /roles/:slug authorized project-role deletion with only assertCanManageRoleType (role:manage, or role:manageProject for roleType=project) and then passed the caller-controlled reassignRoleSlug query string into RoleService.removeCustomRole. The service required the target to exist and to have the same roleType as the deleted role, then RoleRepository.reassignUsersAndRemove updated every matching ProjectRelation.role in one transaction. Because project:admin is a same-type built-in project role, a user with only the narrow global scope role:manageProject could delete any in-use custom project role and reassign its holders instance-wide to project:admin, taking administrative control of projects they were not entitled to manage. The 2.33.4/2.34.1 patch refuses reassignment unless the role is global and the caller has role:manage plus user:changeRole (and is not deleting their own role), and the DTO accepts only assignable global role slugs.",
